WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.900
Welcome to Deck General and Safety.

2
00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.700
The Rules module was about not hitting anybody.

3
00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:14.800
This one is about everything else it takes to run a safe, legal charter, and it starts with the piece of paper you’re studying for.

4
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:18.575
So what does a six-pack license actually let you do?

5
00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:22.025
It lets you carry up to six passengers for hire.

6
00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:24.600
That’s where the nickname comes from.

7
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.600
And only on an uninspected vessel.

8
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.825
Where you can go depends on your endorsement.

9
00:00:31.075 --> 00:00:34.800
Near Coastal takes you up to one hundred miles offshore.

10
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:38.175
Inland keeps you inside the boundary line.

11
00:00:38.425 --> 00:00:44.050
The credential is good for five years, and you renew it through the National Maritime Center.

12
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.925
Now the limit.

13
00:00:46.175 --> 00:00:49.550
What if a seventh paying passenger wants to come along?

14
00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.350
You can’t take him.

15
00:00:52.600 --> 00:01:00.200
Seven or more passengers for hire means an inspected vessel, with a Certificate of Inspection, and a Master license.

16
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.500
Six is a hard number.
